    ["Choose the best word: 'You need a key to open the ______.'","Which word fits?","door","river","cloud","sand","A","A key commonly opens a door.","Match the object with its usual function."],
    ["Choose the best word: 'The doctor told him to drink more ______.'","Which word fits?","water","chairs","shoes","music","A","Water is a drink and fits the health context.","Identify the semantic category before choosing."],
    ["Choose the best word: 'The train arrives at the ______ at 7:30.'","Which word fits?","station","kitchen","forest","pillow","A","A train arrives at a station.","Use the location associated with the subject."],
    ["Choose the correct form: 'She ______ to school every day.'","Which verb is correct?","go","goes","going","gone","B","With third-person singular she, the present simple form is goes.","Check the subject before choosing the verb form."],
    ["Choose the correct form: 'They ______ soccer on Saturdays.'","Which verb is correct?","plays","play","playing","played","B","They takes the base form play in the present simple.","Plural subjects use the base form in present simple."],
    ["Choose the correct form: 'I ______ my homework yesterday.'","Which verb is correct?","finish","finishes","finished","finishing","C","Yesterday signals a completed past action: finished.","Look for time markers such as yesterday."],
    ["Choose the correct form: 'We ______ dinner now.'","Which form is correct?","eat","ate","are eating","eats","C","Now indicates an action in progress: are eating.","'Now' is a strong clue for present continuous."],
    ["Choose the correct preposition: 'The books are ______ the table.'","Which word fits?","on","at","from","between","A","Books resting on a surface are on the table.","Visualize the spatial relation."],
    ["Choose the correct preposition: 'My birthday is ______ July.'","Which word fits?","in","on","at","by","A","Months are used with in.","Use in for months, years and broad periods."],
    ["Choose the correct option: 'I have lived here ______ 2020.'","Which word fits?","for","since","during","from","B","Since introduces a starting point in time.","Since + starting point; for + duration."],
    ["Choose the correct option: 'I have lived here ______ six years.'","Which word fits?","since","for","at","on","B","Six years is a duration, so for is correct.","Duration = for."],
    ["Conversation: 'Would you like some tea?'","Choose the most natural answer.","Yes, please.","At five o'clock.","I am seventeen.","It is across the street.","A","A polite offer is naturally answered with acceptance or refusal.","Match the response to the function of the question."],
    ["Conversation: 'Excuse me, where is the library?'","Choose the best answer.","It is next to the bank.","I am a student.","Yes, I like books.","At seven years old.","A","The question asks for a location.","Identify whether the speaker asks where, when, who or why."],
    ["Conversation: 'How often do you exercise?'","Choose the best answer.","Three times a week.","At the gym.","Because I am tired.","Yesterday.","A","How often asks about frequency.","Frequency expressions answer how often."],
    ["Conversation: 'Why are you late?'","Choose the best answer.","Because the bus was delayed.","At the station.","Three kilometers.","On Monday.","A","Why asks for a reason.","Look for because or another causal explanation."],
    ["Sign: 'KEEP THE DOOR CLOSED'","Where would you most likely see it?","At a room that should remain closed.","At a public swimming pool only.","On a food menu.","Inside a dictionary.","A","The sign gives an instruction about a door.","Signs are understood through the action they request."],
    ["Sign: 'NO PARKING'","What does it mean?","You must not leave a vehicle there.","You must wash the vehicle there.","You can buy a vehicle there.","You should wait for a bus there.","A","No parking prohibits leaving a vehicle in that area.","Focus on the action that is prohibited."],
    ["Notice: 'PLEASE RECYCLE PAPER AND PLASTIC.'","What is the purpose?","To encourage recycling.","To sell paper.","To describe a factory.","To announce a concert.","A","The notice requests an environmental action.","Identify the intended behavior."],
    ["Read: 'Laura missed the first bus, so she arrived at work twenty minutes late.'","Why was Laura late?","She missed the first bus.","She worked twenty minutes less.","The office was closed.","She arrived before the bus.","A","The sentence directly gives the cause.","Use explicit causal connectors such as so."],
    ["Read: 'The park was closed because workers were repairing the playground.'","What can be inferred?","Visitors could not use the park during the repair.","The playground was never used.","Workers closed every park in the city.","The park had no playground.","A","The closure is linked to repair work.","Infer only what follows from the stated information."],
    ["Read: 'Tom bought a jacket because the weather was getting colder.'","Why did Tom buy the jacket?","Because the weather was getting colder.","Because he was going swimming.","Because the shop was closed.","Because summer had arrived.","A","The text gives the reason directly.","Look for because and the clause that follows it."],
    ["Read: 'The museum opens at 9 a.m. and closes at 5 p.m. from Tuesday to Sunday.'","When is it closed according to the notice?","On Monday.","On Wednesday.","At noon.","Every afternoon.","A","The opening days are Tuesday through Sunday, so Monday is excluded.","Pay attention to ranges of days."],
    ["Read: 'Although the apartment is small, it has a large balcony and receives plenty of sunlight.'","Which statement is true?","The apartment is small but has a large balcony.","The apartment is large and dark.","The balcony is smaller than the apartment.","It receives no sunlight.","A","The sentence contrasts small size with a large balcony and good sunlight.","Although introduces a contrast."],
    ["Grammar: 'If it rains tomorrow, we ______ at home.'","Choose the best option.","stay","will stay","stayed","staying","B","First conditional: If + present, will + base verb.","Recognize common conditional patterns."],
    ["Grammar: 'There ______ two books on the desk.'","Choose the best option.","is","are","was","be","B","Two books is plural, so are is required.","Match there is/are with the noun number."],
    ["Grammar: 'My brother is ______ than me.'","Choose the correct word.","tall","taller","tallest","more tall","B","A short adjective uses -er for the comparative.","Look for than as a comparative clue."],
    ["Grammar: 'This is the ______ movie I have seen this year.'","Choose the correct word.","good","better","best","well","C","With 'the' and comparison within a group, the superlative best fits.","Superlative forms often follow 'the'."],
    ["Functional language: 'Could you help me carry this box?'","Choose the best response.","Sure, no problem.","It is Tuesday.","I am from Cali.","At eight o'clock.","A","The question is a request for help.","Match the response to the social function."],
    ["Functional language: 'I'm sorry I broke the cup.'","Choose the most appropriate response.","That's okay. Be careful next time.","Where is the cup?","At three o'clock.","I have two cups.","A","An apology is naturally answered by accepting or responding to it.","Recognize apology and response patterns."],
    ["Functional language: 'Congratulations on your new job!'","Choose the best response.","Thank you!","Because it was raining.","At the station.","No, I don't.","A","Congratulations is a positive social expression, so Thank you is natural.","Identify the communicative function before reading every option."],
    ["Read: 'The community garden started with ten volunteers. Six months later, more than thirty people were participating every weekend.'","What changed?","The number of participants increased.","The garden closed.","Only ten people remained.","Volunteers stopped meeting.","A","The passage contrasts ten volunteers with more than thirty participants.","Compare quantities across time."],
    ["Read: 'The school installed solar panels to reduce electricity costs and use renewable energy.'","Why did the school install them?","To reduce costs and use renewable energy.","To increase paper consumption.","To close the school.","To replace all teachers.","A","The text states both purposes.","When two reasons are stated, choose the option that preserves both."],
    ["Read: 'Nina wanted to run in the race, but she injured her ankle the day before.'","What happened?","Her ankle injury prevented her from being able to run normally.","She won the race easily.","She trained for another month.","The race was canceled.","A","The injury is the relevant event affecting her plan.","Do not add outcomes not stated."]
